---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Transform from '../components/Transform.jsx';
---
<Base path="/crop-image/" title="Crop Images Online — Drag to Crop JPG, PNG, WebP | PlainMile" description="Crop JPG, PNG and WebP images in your browser. Drag a selection or choose square, 4:3, 16:9 and portrait ratios, then download without uploading photos.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Image tools</a> / Crop image</p>
    <h1>Crop an image by dragging a frame</h1>
    <p class="lead">Choose a picture, drag the crop box over what you want to keep and download the result. No account, upload or extra editing steps.</p>
  </section>
  <Transform client:load lang="en" tool="crop"/>
  <section class="reference" aria-label="Image crop help">
    <h2>Choose a crop area visually</h2>
    <p>Crop a screenshot, remove unwanted edges or frame a profile picture. Choose a free crop, square (1:1), landscape (4:3), widescreen (16:9) or portrait (3:4) ratio. Move the box by dragging inside it, resize from the bottom-right corner or draw another box outside it. Exact pixel coordinates are optional. After exporting, you can drag the frame again and generate an updated result without reselecting the file.</p>
    <p>The result contains only the pixels inside the selected frame. Cropping does not stretch the photo or guarantee the exact pixel size required by an upload form. To resize afterward, use <a href="/resize-image/">Resize image</a>; to meet a file-size limit, use <a href="/compress-image-to-size/">Compress to KB</a>.</p>
    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <ol><li>Choose one JPG, PNG or WebP image, or paste a screenshot.</li><li>Select a shape if useful, then drag or resize the crop frame to keep the right area.</li><li>Choose the output format if needed, click Crop image, then download the result.</li></ol>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <div class="qa"><h3>How do I crop a square profile picture?</h3><p>Choose Square (1:1), move the crop frame over your subject and adjust its size. The downloaded image will be square; check whether the destination requires a minimum pixel resolution.</p></div>
    <div class="qa"><h3>Does cropping change image dimensions?</h3><p>Yes. The exported pixel width and height are the selected crop area, not the original full image size. The output dimensions appear before download.</p></div>
    <div class="qa"><h3>Can I keep a transparent PNG background?</h3><p>Yes. Keep the original PNG format or choose WebP. JPG cannot preserve transparency and replaces transparent areas with white.</p></div>
    <div class="qa"><h3>Are animated images supported?</h3><p>No. Animated PNG/WebP inputs are rejected instead of losing their additional animation frames.</p></div>
    <h2>Other image tools</h2>
    <ul class="related-links"><li><a href="/rotate-image/">Rotate or flip an image</a></li><li><a href="/convert-image/">Convert JPG, PNG, WebP</a></li><li><a href="/resize-image/">Resize an image</a></li></ul>
    <p class="editor-disclosure">Cropping takes place only in your browser. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
